content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Archivist",
      "description": "Person who evaluates and organizes incoming documents"
    },
    {
      "name": "Document",
      "description": "Any item stored in the archive with descriptive metadata",
      "attributes": [
        "Metadata"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Metadata",
      "description": "Descriptive information created to help locate a Document"
    },
    {
      "name": "Collection",
      "description": "Group of related Documents organized for easier access",
      "attributes": [
        "Document"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Records Manager",
      "description": "Person who oversees municipal records and keeps filing procedures in order"
    },
    {
      "name": "Municipal Record",
      "description": "Official record maintained by the municipality"
    },
    {
      "name": "Digital Archive",
      "description": "Online archive storing Documents digitally",
      "attributes": [
        "Document"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Person who helps visitors find documents and prepares research copies"
    },
    {
      "name": "Copy",
      "description": "Reproduced version of a Document for research or legal use"
    },
    {
      "name": "Public Services Officer",
      "description": "Person who handles citizen inquiries and coordinates Document Requests"
    },
    {
      "name": "Citizen Inquiry",
      "description": "Question submitted by a Citizen about how to find or access records"
    },
    {
      "name": "Document Request",
      "description": "Formal request for access to specific documents"
    },
    {
      "name": "Citizen",
      "description": "Individual who searches catalogs and requests documents"
    },
    {
      "name": "Access Request",
      "description": "Request submitted by a Citizen to obtain access to a Document"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Archiving": {
      "objects": [
        "Archivist",
        "Document",
        "Metadata",
        "Collection",
        "Records Manager",
        "Municipal Record",
        "Digital Archive"
      ]
    },
    "Researching": {
      "objects": [
        "Citizen",
        "Research Assistant",
        "Public Services Officer",
        "Copy",
        "Access Request",
        "Document Request",
        "Citizen Inquiry"
      ]
    },
    "subdomain connections": [
      "Archiving--Researching"
    ]
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Archiving": {
      "derived from": "Archiving Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Archivist",
        "Document",
        "Metadata",
        "Collection",
        "Records Manager",
        "Municipal Record",
        "Digital Archive"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Researching": {
      "derived from": "Researching Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Citizen",
        "Research Assistant",
        "Public Services Officer",
        "Copy",
        "Access Request",
        "Document Request",
        "Citizen Inquiry"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
